1. Product Overview
1.1 Product Vision
To make literature accessible across language barriers and create an immersive, personalized reading experience while empowering publishers to distribute, monetize, and understand their content globally.
1.2 Product Summary
NOVELIA is a multilingual digital reading marketplace connecting readers and publishers worldwide. Readers can discover, purchase, and read digital books, manage their libraries, participate in chapter-based discussions, and use ROX, an AI-powered assistant. Publishers can upload and manage books, monitor performance and earnings, and submit promotional campaigns through the Reach Readers feature.
1.3 Product Value Proposition
•	Discover: Find books by title, author, genre, language, and other preferences.
•	Experience: Read with optional instrumental background music and chapter-based community discussions.
•	Manage: Use ROX AI to assist with reading, searching, purchasing reminders, publishing workflows, and analytics.
•	Connect: Give publishers tools to distribute books and understand aggregate reader engagement.
2. Problem Statement and Objectives
2.1 Problem Statement
Readers may face language barriers when accessing international literature, have fragmented tools for managing purchases and reading progress, and lack immersive or chapter-specific community experiences. Publishers may lack an integrated platform for distributing digital books, monitoring sales and engagement, and requesting promotional support.
2.2 Product Objectives
•	Provide a centralized marketplace for digital books and approved language editions.
•	Make it easy for readers to discover, purchase, and manage books.
•	Improve reading engagement through StorySound and Chapter Circle.
•	Provide publishers with book management, sales, earnings, and engagement insights.
•	Use ROX to simplify high-value reader and publisher tasks.
•	Establish a scalable foundation for global distribution and future monetization.
3. Target Users and Personas
User type	Description	Primary needs
Global reader	A person who reads digital books and may prefer one or more languages.	Discover books, access preferred language editions, purchase, read, and manage a library.
Book enthusiast	A frequent reader who tracks progress and follows authors or genres.	Reading history, favorites, recommendations, upcoming releases, and community.
Independent author	An individual who publishes and sells their own work.	Upload and manage books, track performance, receive earnings, and promote books.
Publishing company	An organization managing multiple authors or titles.	Manage a catalog, schedule releases, analyze performance, and manage payments.
Platform administrator	An authorized NOVELIA operator.	Verify publishers, moderate content, approve books and campaigns, and oversee platform operations.

4. User Roles and Access
Role	Main capabilities
Reader	Browse books, purchase, read, manage library and preferences, join chapter discussions, use StorySound, and interact with ROX.
Publisher	Manage publisher profile and books, schedule releases, view analytics and earnings, submit Reach Readers campaigns, and use ROX.
Administrator	Manage users and publishers, approve books, review campaigns, oversee payments, moderate discussions, and monitor platform activity.

Access must be role-based. Readers must not access publisher or admin functions. Publishers must only manage their own organization and books. Administrators must have controlled access to operational and moderation functions.
5. Scope and Release Strategy
5.1 MVP Scope
•	Reader, publisher, and administrator demo access and role-based navigation.
•	Reader home, book discovery, search, filters, book details, library, favorites, and reading progress.
•	Simulated book purchase and transaction history.
•	Basic reading interface with bookmarks and automatic progress saving.
•	StorySound with predefined, licensed or original instrumental tracks.
•	Chapter Circle discussion popup and basic chapter-specific comments.
•	Publisher dashboard, book upload form, book management, and basic analytics.
•	Publisher earnings and payment history using sample or simulated data.
•	Reach Readers campaign request submission and admin review.
•	Basic role-aware ROX assistant with selected reader and publisher use cases.
•	Basic admin functions for publisher, book, campaign, and community moderation.
5.2 Future Scope
•	Production payment gateway integration and real publisher payouts.
•	AI-assisted translation and publisher-approved multilingual editions.
•	Advanced personalized recommendations.
•	AI-generated or dynamically adaptive soundtracks.
•	Advanced publisher analytics and reader segmentation.
•	Automated notifications across email, push, and in-app channels.
•	Audiobooks, social reading clubs, and author-reader events.
•	Advanced digital rights management (DRM) and content protection.
5.3 Out of Scope for Initial Prototype
•	Real-money payment processing.
•	Guaranteed production-grade DRM.
•	Unreviewed AI translation of complete commercial books.
•	Autonomous AI actions that spend money or publish content without confirmation.
•	Native iOS and Android applications.
6. Functional Requirements — Reader Portal
6.1 Authentication and Onboarding
•	Readers can register using email and password.
•	Readers can log in, log out, and recover a forgotten password.
•	Readers can manage profile information.
•	Onboarding allows selection of preferred reading language, genres, and interests.
•	Readers can update language and notification preferences.
6.2 Book Discovery and Marketplace
•	Browse available books by category, genre, popularity, and release date.
•	Search by title, author, publisher, genre, language, and keyword.
•	Filter by language, genre, price, and release date.
•	View book cover, description, author, publisher, language, release date, price, and available editions.
•	View ratings and reviews where enabled.
•	Add and remove books from favorites or wishlist.
•	View upcoming releases and follow books or authors.
•	Display original and translated editions as distinct editions with clear language labels.
Language requirement clarification: the product must distinguish between a publisher-uploaded/approved translated edition and an AI-generated translation. The initial commercial release should prioritize authorized, publisher-approved editions.
6.3 Book Purchasing and Pricing
Readers can purchase individual digital books. The platform displays a launch price during the first seven days after a book's release and the regular price thereafter.
Pricing period	Proposed demo price	Status
First seven days after release	USD 2.00	Assumption for prototype; client confirmation required
After the first seven days	USD 4.00	Assumption for prototype; client confirmation required

•	Calculate the applicable price using the book's release timestamp and configured promotional period.
•	Display the price, applicable promotion, and order summary before checkout.
•	Record purchase status and make successfully purchased books available in My Library.
•	Show purchase confirmation and transaction history.
•	Support transaction states such as pending, successful, failed, refunded, and cancelled in the production design.
•	Real purchases must require explicit reader confirmation and secure payment processing.
6.4 Reader Dashboard
Dashboard section	Requirement
My Library	List all purchased and accessible books.
Reading Progress	Show current book, chapter, last-read position, and completion percentage.
Favorites	Show books saved as favorites.
Wishlist	Show books saved for future purchase.
Subscriptions	Show active, expired, and available subscription plans.
Payments	Show transaction history, status, amount, date, and receipt where applicable.
Upcoming Releases	Show followed books and upcoming launch dates.
Notifications	Show purchase, release, subscription, and community updates.
Reading History	Show recently opened and previously read books.

6.5 Reading Experience
•	Open and read purchased books in a chapter-based reader.
•	Support adjustable font size, light/dark themes, and readable typography.
•	Support chapter navigation, bookmarks, and text highlighting where technically supported.
•	Save reading position and progress automatically.
•	Allow searching within the book by keyword or phrase.
•	Allow the reader to switch between available authorized language editions.
•	Ensure the reading experience is responsive on desktop, tablet, and mobile.
6.6 StorySound — Immersive Background Music
StorySound is an optional instrumental audio experience that allows readers to play background music associated with a book or chapter.
•	Display an on/off control within the reading interface.
•	Support play, pause, volume adjustment, and track selection where available.
•	Associate predefined instrumental tracks or moods with individual chapters.
•	Use non-lyrical music only in the initial feature scope.
•	Change tracks at chapter transitions when a new chapter mood is configured.
•	Pause or stop playback when the reader exits the book or disables StorySound.
•	Respect the reader's audio preferences and avoid unexpected playback.
Story atmosphere	Example audio mood
Romantic	Soft piano or gentle strings
Mystery	Suspenseful ambient instrumental
Action	Cinematic instrumental
Sad or reflective	Emotional piano
Peaceful	Nature-inspired ambient

MVP recommendation: use a curated set of licensed or original audio tracks mapped to chapter moods. AI-generated adaptive soundtracks are a future enhancement.
6.7 Chapter Circle — Chapter Discussions
After a reader completes a chapter, the platform may display a discussion prompt: “Share your feelings till now before the break....”
•	Display a popup after chapter completion.
•	Allow readers to submit chapter-specific comments.
•	Allow readers to view comments from other eligible readers.
•	Support replies and reactions in a later MVP iteration if needed.
•	Allow readers to skip the discussion and continue reading.
•	Restrict discussion visibility to avoid spoilers from chapters the reader has not unlocked.
•	Allow users to report inappropriate comments.
•	Provide administrator moderation and content removal capabilities.
6.8 Reader Notifications
•	Upcoming release reminders for followed books or authors.
•	New release notifications.
•	Purchase confirmations and payment status updates.
•	Subscription renewal or expiry reminders.
•	Replies and reactions to chapter discussions.
•	Allow readers to configure notification preferences and frequency.
6.9 ROX AI — Reader Assistant
ROX is the in-app AI assistant. In the reader portal, ROX helps users discover, understand, search, and manage their reading activities.
Use case	Example prompt or action
In-book search	Find the chapter or passage containing a specific keyword.
Chapter lookup	Find the chapter where a named event or character interaction occurs.
Reading support	Explain a passage or summarize chapters the reader has completed.
Recommendations	Recommend books based on genres or reading history.
Purchase reminder	Remind me to purchase this book on Friday.
Reading insights	Show my reading progress this month.

•	ROX must respect the reader's account permissions and purchased content access.
•	ROX must respect reading progress and spoiler boundaries by default.
•	ROX must ground book-related answers in available book content and identify uncertainty.
•	Scheduled purchases must be reminders or pending actions; no payment may be charged without explicit confirmation.
•	The prototype may use mock responses; production requires secure AI integration and usage controls.
7. Functional Requirements — Publisher Portal
7.1 Publisher Registration and Verification
•	Support registration as an individual author or publishing organization.
•	Collect publisher name, contact details, organization type, and relevant profile information.
•	Allow submission of verification documents where required.
•	Allow publishers to provide payout details through a secure process.
•	Support pending, approved, rejected, and suspended verification states.
•	Require approval before a publisher can make books publicly available.
7.2 Publisher Dashboard
•	Display total books published and books awaiting approval.
•	Display total units sold, gross revenue, estimated publisher earnings, and pending payouts.
•	Display total and active readers where measurable.
•	Highlight best-performing books and recent transactions.
•	Display upcoming scheduled releases.
•	Provide links to book performance and payment details.
7.3 Book Management
•	Add a book with title, subtitle, description, author, genre, language, and metadata.
•	Upload book cover and manuscript files in supported formats such as EPUB and PDF.
•	Add chapter structure and chapter metadata.
•	Set release date, launch price, and regular price.
•	Configure StorySound track or mood by chapter where available.
•	Save a book as draft and submit it for review.
•	Edit book details subject to publication and approval rules.
•	Archive or request removal of a book.
•	View book approval status and administrator feedback.
Content retention rule: removing or delisting a book must not automatically revoke access for readers who already purchased it. The platform must define contractual, copyright, and legal exceptions before production.
7.4 Book Performance Analytics
Metric	Definition
Total sales	Number of completed purchases for the book.
Gross revenue	Total value of completed sales before deductions.
Publisher earnings	Amount payable to the publisher after commissions and adjustments.
Active readers	Readers who have recently engaged with the book, based on a defined activity window.
Completion rate	Percentage of readers who reach the defined completion point.
Chapter engagement	Reading activity or completion by chapter.
Ratings	Average rating and number of ratings, where enabled.
Favorites	Number of readers who saved the book.

7.5 Publisher Payments and Earnings
•	Show total earnings and earnings by book.
•	Show individual transactions with date, book, gross amount, commission, adjustments, and net amount.
•	Show pending, processing, completed, failed, and reversed payout statuses where applicable.
•	Allow publishers to view and download payment statements.
•	Show platform commission and refund adjustments transparently.
•	Provide payout history and payout details.
Illustrative revenue-share example: for a USD 4.00 sale and a 20% platform commission, the platform commission is USD 0.80 and the publisher share is USD 3.20 before any other applicable adjustments. The commission rate and settlement terms require client approval.
7.6 Reach Readers — Promotional Campaign Requests
Reach Readers allows a publisher to request promotional support from NOVELIA.
•	Provide a Reach Readers action for each eligible book.
•	Open a campaign request form with selected book, campaign type, target audience, target language/region, objectives, proposed dates, and optional notes.
•	Allow publishers to submit and track campaign requests.
•	Notify administrators when a request is submitted.
•	Allow administrators to approve, reject, request changes, schedule, and close campaigns.
•	Display campaign status to the publisher.
Campaign status	Meaning
Draft	Publisher has not submitted the request.
Submitted	Request has been sent to the platform.
Under Review	Administrator is evaluating the request.
Approved	Campaign is approved and can be scheduled.
Rejected	Request is declined with a reason where appropriate.
Active	Campaign is currently running.
Completed	Campaign has ended.

7.7 ROX AI — Publisher Assistant
Use case	Example prompt or action
Release scheduling	Schedule my new book for a specified date.
Sales analysis	Which of my books generated the highest revenue this month?
Engagement analysis	Analyze reader engagement and completion for my latest book.
Content support	Generate a draft book description from the supplied metadata.
Promotion planning	Suggest a campaign for my mystery novel.
Market insight	Which genres or languages show stronger engagement in my available aggregate data?

•	ROX must only access data the publisher is authorized to view.
•	Publisher analytics must distinguish measured results from AI-generated estimates or recommendations.
•	ROX must not expose personally identifiable reader data unless a lawful, explicit product policy permits it.
•	Actions such as scheduling a release or submitting a campaign require confirmation before execution.
•	AI-generated descriptions and campaign content must be reviewable and editable before publication.
8. Functional Requirements — Admin Portal
Module	Requirements
User management	View, activate, suspend, and manage reader accounts according to policy.
Publisher management	Review verification details; approve, reject, or suspend publisher accounts.
