9. Business Rules
ID	Business rule
BR-01	Readers must register or log in before purchasing a book.
BR-02	The launch price applies during the first seven days after the configured release time.
BR-03	The regular price applies after the launch promotional period ends.
BR-04	The regular price must be configurable; USD 4.00 is only a proposed prototype assumption.
BR-05	Purchased books must appear in the reader's library after successful payment confirmation.
BR-06	Reading progress must be saved automatically.
BR-07	Chapter discussions must be associated with a specific book and chapter.
BR-08	Discussion access must follow spoiler and chapter-access rules.
BR-09	Publishers may manage only books and data belonging to their own publisher account.
BR-10	Books must pass the required approval process before public availability.
BR-11	Publisher earnings must account for commissions, refunds, and adjustments.
BR-12	Reach Readers campaigns require administrator approval.
BR-13	ROX must follow role-based access and data privacy rules.
BR-14	ROX must not execute a purchase or charge a payment method without explicit confirmation.
BR-15	Translated editions must have appropriate distribution and translation rights.
BR-16	Delisting a book must not automatically remove access for existing purchasers, subject to legal and licensing obligations.

